  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `reckon/crew/promotion_requests.py` (failure_obligations at 1403), `reckon/crew/obligation_snapshot.py` (`_payload_for_state` at 2178, called at 2288), `reckon/crew/review.py` (`added_failures_from_gate_logs` at 3291, `_gate_log_format` at 2755) all resolve to the lines cited, and the two declared write-path modules exist.",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 s104's decode bound cannot hold for the requests its own read settles, so the done-when is unsatisfiable as written.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 both sections put gate logs and arm logs under the run directory with the `# command:`/`EXIT=` convention, and the cited profile `~/.cache/reckon-landing/station-prof-post-s102.raw` is present and readable (639,859 bytes).",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 section titles and deliverables name the mechanism (\"a publish reads each promotion request once\", \"an unchanged gate-log pair is counted once\"), carrying no plan labels, stage names or ticket numbers.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 both sections' root causes match the cited profile exactly, but each states its implementation mechanism in plan text (`file_memo` in s104's deliverable, `_gate_log_format` in s105's done-when).",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 s104 delivers one publish that reads each promotion request at most once, s105 one added-failure count per unchanged log pair; neither carries a second independently closable deliverable.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 the snapshot's `plan-section-depends-on` now carries `s104` and `s105` waiting on `the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once#s96` (the only landed section either builds on), both sections exist as `#s104`/`#s105` and declare `implementable`, and no declared edge points at a section that does not exist."
  },
